Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-29-2001||10:47 PM||||  Looking in to some bolt on's and was thinking about the underdrive pulley from the Fiero Store. Is it compatable with the 3.4L engine? Also, what type of ignition would yield additional HP and approximately how much? I have heard that an MSD system would help, any thoughts? I'm still looking for the best headers to use. Are there any after market cam setups that work well with the 3.4? I was going to have the new heads ported and all of that but the guy at the "RECOMENDED" machine shop told me not to waste my time for a street car. He told me that all that work and I would lose alot of bottom end torque and that after a couple of months, all the polishing and porting would be worthless (carbon). That is of course, taking into consideration that it will be my daily driver. He recomended a good moderate cam (if available) hearders, upgraded exhaust, increased intake, underdrive pulley, and a hot ignition. Any thoughts? TIA<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||04-29-2001||11:33 PM||||MSD will not add horsepower. Ignition is binary. You either get it or not. MSD is only good for ENSURING that you get a spark. This means that it eliminates power LOSS. You shouldn't get any real gains, just more predictable performance across the powerband.||||reg||6
Z||000002||87GTZ34||04-30-2001||02:01 AM||||BB Your machine shop guy is making sense.  Its all about what RPM range you want the power and torque at.  If you build the most HP possible, it will be in the upper RPM range and the car won't be much fun to drive on the street.  That is unless you like speeding tickets and have a stick and are willing to drive in 1 & 2.  The pieces you seek are all available so yo just need to ask around for opinions (and dyno slips) and then shop prices.||||reg||1
